1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The Great Barrier Reef is the largest living structure on Earth, visible from outer space.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,000
It stretches over two thousand three hundred kilometers along the coast of Queensland, Australia.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:16,000
This underwater paradise is composed of nearly three thousand individual reef systems and nine hundred islands.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,000
The reef is home to an extraordinary diversity of marine life, including over fifteen hundred species of fish.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:26,000
Sea turtles, dolphins, sharks, and manta rays all inhabit these vibrant coral waters.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,000
The corals themselves are living organisms, comprising colonies of tiny animals called polyps.

7
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Climate change poses the single greatest threat to the reef's survival.

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,000
Rising ocean temperatures cause coral bleaching, which can be fatal if sustained.

9
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,000
Despite these challenges, parts of the reef remain remarkably resilient and continue to regenerate.

10
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:52,000
Scientists and conservationists around the world are working together to protect this natural wonder.

